; Direct tests of the helpers the stages share: the traversals of the TST and
; the CGT (traversals.ml), types and their substitution,
; signatures, overload ranking, lowering's type layouts, what stage 5's
; evaluator makes of the tree, how codegen reads a snapshot, and the processor
; codegen tunes for and which targets it accepts. The golden suites test the
; same code end to end; these say which helper broke, rather than where in a
; golden file the difference surfaced. They also check that semantics run twice in one process gives the
; same tree (it keeps no numbering from one check to the next), that the
; test rules' generator pairs every fixture with a golden file, and that the
; driver checks a stamp and keeps a file its rewrite did not create.
;
; Overloads, State, Type_layout, Emit, Build and stage 5's modules are not re-exported by their libraries'
; entry modules, so they are reached by the names dune gives them.

(test
 (name unit)
 (libraries cgt codegen diagnostic driver fixture_pairing llvm llvm.target optimize source sst tree_graph tst unix)
 (deps
  ../../runtime/zane.h
  (source_tree ../codegen/fixtures/lambdas)))
